   "text": "This SMILES was read region by region from the drawing. I did not run it through a parser, so the validity check was done by hand.\n\n- **Left end:** a pyrazine-2-carboxamide with a piperidin-1-yl group and an anilino NH. The aniline ring carries a 4-piperidinyl group, and that piperidine nitrogen starts a \u2013CH2CH2OCH2CH2OCH2C(=O)\u2013 linker.\n- **Centre:** a tert-leucine amide joined to a 4-hydroxyproline amide, then a benzylamide. The benzene ring has the thiazole para to the CH2 and the ether oxygen ortho. The thiazole is 4-methylthiazol-5-yl. I took the stereocentres as the standard VHL-ligand configuration, matching the wedges and hashes drawn. I checked the neighbour order of each centre against the standard form of that ligand.\n- **Right end:** the ether oxygen continues through \u2013CH2CH2OCH2CH2N(CH3)CH2\u2013 to a cyclohexane. The cyclohexane is drawn trans-1,4 (one wedge, one hash) and is bonded to N2 of a 2H-indazole. The indazole carries the 6-(2-hydroxypropan-2-yl) group and, at C5, an amide to 6-(trifluoromethyl)picolinic acid.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)c1ncc(N2CCCCC2)nc1Nc1ccc(cc1)C1CCN(CC1)CCOCCOCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N1C[C@H](O)C[C@H]1C(=O)NCc1ccc(cc1OCCOCCN(C)C[C@H]1CC[C@@H](CC1)n1cc2cc(NC(=O)c3cccc(n3)C(F)(F)F)c(C(C)(C)O)cc2n1)-c1scnc1C"
